.TH APERI-SETUP 1 2026-11-15 "aperi @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aperi-setup \- configure a user account to use aperi
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aperi-setup
.RI [ option ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aperi-setup
configures the account of the user running it to use
.BR aperi (1)
and
.BR aperi-session (1).
It performs the steps below, in order.
For each step it shows what it is going to do and asks for confirmation,
unless
.B \-\-yes
is given.
.PP
It never overwrites the aperi configuration, and every file it replaces is
first backed up as
.IR file .bak- timestamp .
Running it again on an account already set up changes nothing.
.PP
Every change, with the backups made, is appended with a timestamp to the
log file
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/aperi/setup.log ,
together with the start of each run, its options and how it ended
(finished, failed or interrupted).
If the log can't be written a warning is printed and the setup goes on.
.SH STEPS
.TP
.B config
Create
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/aperi/config
from the example configuration, if it doesn't exist.
Its rules must then be adapted to the programs you use.
.TP
.B mimeapps
Make aperi the default application for the common MIME types in
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mimeapps.list .
If the file already exists, ask whether to merge the aperi associations
keeping the existing defaults (the default answer), merge them replacing the
existing defaults, back up and replace the file, or skip the step; with
.B \-\-yes
the file is backed up and replaced.
Only the
.B [Default Applications]
section is changed by a merge.
Then make the deprecated
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/applications/mimeapps.list
a link to it.
.TP
.B xdg-open
Link
.I ~/.local/bin/xdg-open
to
.BR aperi ,
to use it in place of
.BR xdg-open (1),
and warn if it's not the first
.B xdg-open
in
.BR PATH .
An existing
.I ~/.local/bin/xdg-open
that isn't such a link is replaced only after confirmation, never with
.BR \-\-yes .
.TP
.B session
Ask how to start
.B aperi-session
at login: enable the
.B aperi-session.service
systemd user unit (starting it if a graphical session is active), print the
line to add to the compositor startup commands, or nothing.
With
.B \-\-yes
the unit is used if a systemd user manager is running, otherwise the
compositor line is printed.
Compositor configuration files are never modified.
.TP
.B show-items
Install the example
.I show_items.py
in
.I ~/.local/bin
and add an
.B aperi-show-items://
rule using it to the aperi configuration, before the catch all
.B /*
rule if there is one.
The rule uses the absolute path of the script, since the
.B PATH
of the systemd user manager usually doesn't contain
.IR ~/.local/bin .
Warn about the missing programs the script needs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Don't ask: use the default answers.
Without this option the standard input must be a terminal.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-skip " \fIstep\fR"
Skip
.IR step .
Can be repeated.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-only " \fIstep\fR"
Run only
.IR step .
Can be repeated.
.TP
.BR \-\-session " \fBsystemd\fR|\fBcompositor\fR|\fBnone\fR"
How to start
.BR aperi-session ,
without asking.
.TP
.BR \-\-examples " \fIdirectory\fR"
Take the example files from
.I directory
instead of
.IR @EXAMPLESDIR@ ,
e.g.\& the
.I extra
directory of the aperi source tree.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory of the aperi configuration and of
.I mimeapps.list
.RI ( ~/.config
if not set).
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Base directory of the log file
.RI ( ~/.local/state
if not set).
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directory of the deprecated
.I mimeapps.list
location
.RI ( ~/.local/share
if not set).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/aperi/setup.log
The log of the changes made.
.TP
.I @EXAMPLESDIR@/
The example
.IR config ,
.I mimeapps.list
and
.I show_items.py
files.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on errors or invalid options.
.SH EXAMPLES
Set up everything, answering each question:
.PP
.RS
.EX
aperi-setup
.EE
.RE
.PP
Set up everything but the xdg-open link without asking, starting
.B aperi-session
from the compositor:
.PP
.RS
.EX
aperi-setup \-\-yes \-\-skip xdg-open \-\-session compositor
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aperi (1),
.BR aperi-session (1),
.BR xdg-mime (1)
.SH AUTHORS
Matteo Beniamino <m.beniamino@tautologica.org>
